From 5616471e46ee5e6317c4a2b188f7a87ade263944 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 15:25:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: free-text-first answer flow for exercises and contest
 questions
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Pairs with the backend patch that adds reponseTexte + the check-answer
endpoints. When an exercise/question has a configured answer, students
now see a free-text field first instead of jumping straight to multiple
choice:

- Up to 4 free-text tries (client-tracked), each checked server-side via
  the new check-answer endpoint. A correct guess on any try earns full XP
  (no hint penalty — nothing's been revealed yet) and shows the solution
  immediately.
- After 4 wrong tries, falls straight through to the existing hints +
  multiple-choice flow, completely unchanged — same components, same XP
  penalty tiers, same submission endpoint. Content with no configured
  free-text answer skips straight to today's behavior, so this is fully
  backward compatible.
- Works identically for both the standalone exercise screen and each
  question inside a contest session (state resets correctly between
  questions).
- Wired flutter_math_fork's LatexText (already built, just not connected
  anywhere yet) into every place students actually read exercise/question
  content: énoncé, hints, and solution — for both exercises and contests.
- Admin exercise form and contest-question form both get a new optional
  "Réponse exacte (texte libre)" field so admins can actually configure
  this. Contest question forms only had 2 of 4 hint fields; left as-is
  here to keep this patch focused — worth a follow-up.

Depends on the backend free-text-answer patch (schema migration +
check-answer endpoints) — apply that first.

I don't have a Flutter SDK in this sandbox — reviewed manually (brace/
paren/bracket balance, exact backend response shape matching). Please run
flutter analyze before merging.
